      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Identification of patients with suspect acute coronary syndrome begins from the evaluation of chest pain by the triage nursing. The nurse, through a diligent triage examination, gathers information so that patients undergo an adequate and correct diagnostic-therapeutic process. Once the level of risk is defined, it is very important to determine the welfare program and to follow normal practice of monitoring to prevent and early recognize patients with acute coronary syndrome at high risk."},
